  "texts": {
    "preamble": "M/S Gupta Enterprises vs Sh. Ghanshyam Tewari on 28 February, 2018 In The Court Of Sh. Ajay Gupta, Addl. Sessions Judge02 (East) Spl. Judge (Ndps) Karkardooma Courts, Delhi Cri. Appeal No. 36/17 In the matter of M/s Gupta Enterprises (through Sh. Kripa Shanker Gupta) Shop No.323, Kotla Village, near Shiv Hanuman Mandir, Mayur Vihar, PhaseI, New Delhi91 versus Sh. Ghanshyam Tewari Prop. Of M/s Multi Sales Corp., R/o H.No. H 80, New Seelampur, Delhi Office at: Multi Sales Corporation E45, West Nath Colony, Gali No.3/3, Opp. Hoti Lal Dharamshala, Mandoli Road, Shahdara, Delhi32 .. Date of institution 09.03.2017 Arguments heard 03.02.2018 Date of order 28.02.2018 Judgment",
    "facts": "State filed criminal appeal before the Sessions Court under Section 378(1)(a) Cr.P.C. Preliminary objection regarding maintainability of the appeal before the Sessions Court was rejected. He cannot file such appeal in the Sessions Court. The complainant can challenge the order of acquittal by filing an application for special leave to appeal in the Delhi High Court and not in the Sessions Court....?",
    "arguments": "16. In a recent case 'Bhavuben Dineshbhai Makwana v. State of Gujarat & ors.', 2013 Crl.L.J. 4225, Full Bench of Gujarat High Court answering the reference on question number (3) 'If the victim prefers an appeal before this Court, challenging the acquittal, invoking his right under proviso to Section 372 of Cr.P.C., whether that appellant is required to first seek leave of the Court, as is required in case of appeal being preferred by M/s Gupta Enterprises vs Sh. Ghanshyam Tiwari Cri.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "16. In a recent case 'Bhavuben Dineshbhai Makwana v. State of Gujarat & ors.', 2013 Crl.L.J. 4225, Full Bench of Gujarat High Court answering the reference on question number (3) 'If the victim prefers an appeal before this Court, challenging the acquittal, invoking his right under proviso to Section 372 of Cr.P.C., whether that appellant is required to first seek leave of the Court, as is required in case of appeal being preferred by M/s Gupta Enterprises vs Sh. Ghanshyam Tiwari Cri."
